## CQ-PS15-01
@group client
@commands Compat with the wall-exit lift installed. Portal Gun: floor portal, wall portal; fall through the floor portal 3 times; then walk out of a wall portal 3 times (no fall)
@pass falling into the wall portal: player ends standing in front of the wall, can walk and jump, no `y` inside the floor; walking out: no one-block lift (as 2026-11-14)
@fails read `Adjusting Client Player Position` lines; adjust the in-front test in `IPExitLiftMixin`
@draft portal exit feel (falls and walk-outs judged by a person in the client)
@owner true
## CQ-PS15-02
@group client
@commands Bisect SQ-PG-01c, one change per launch, same save: (1) `fast_buffer_upload: false` in `config/immediatelyfast.json`; (2) `hud_batching: false`; (3) Rubidium and Rubidium Extra out of `mods/`; (4) Distant Horizons out. Light a Flint and Terrasteel Nether portal each time
@pass first change after which the portal renders and the client survives 30 s is the cause; record it
@fails all four still crash: take a fresh hs_err and check `GL_ELEMENT_ARRAY_BUFFER_BINDING` with a GL debug launch
@draft bisect across four launches, each with a config or mods/ change between launches: a person runs it
@owner true
## CQ-PS15-03
@group client
@commands Fly to a Visceral Heap whose edge meets a warped forest (`/locate`); screenshots from 3 sides
@pass spill into the forest reads as a natural border
@fails owner decides: clamp the heap feature to its biome
@draft whether the spill reads as a natural border is the owner's taste
@owner true
## SQ-PS15-01 | salt dust click on ice, packed ice, snow layer (1 and 3): a salt layer on top, target not melted; then the layer melts it
@group A
@commands Salt dust click on ice, packed ice, snow layer (CD 1.1.0 with Salt -04, Common 1.2.0 of 2026-11-15)
@pass a salt layer is placed on top; the ice is not melted by the click; the layer then melts it at block rate
@fails route the click through the layer place only
@from batches/r1116/ps15_a.qb
> setblock 300 -61 300 minecraft:ice
> setblock 303 -61 300 minecraft:packed_ice
> setblock 306 -60 300 minecraft:snow[layers=1]
> setblock 309 -60 300 minecraft:snow[layers=3]
> cdevtest use 300 -61 300 held=vintagedelight:salt_dust*4 face=up
> cdevtest state 300 -60 300
> cdevtest use 303 -61 300 held=vintagedelight:salt_dust*4 face=up
> cdevtest state 303 -60 300
> cdevtest use 306 -60 300 held=vintagedelight:salt_dust*4 face=up
> cdevtest state 306 -59 300
> cdevtest use 309 -60 300 held=vintagedelight:salt_dust*4 face=up
> cdevtest state 309 -59 300
sleep 1
> say ps01 random ticks
> cdevtest randomtick 300 -61 300 300 -61 300 40 nofluids
> cdevtest randomtick 303 -61 300 303 -61 300 200 nofluids
> cdevtest state 300 -61 300
> cdevtest state 300 -60 300
> cdevtest state 303 -61 300
> cdevtest state 303 -60 300
> cdevtest items 304 -60 300 8
count \[cdevtest\] verb=use who=fake hand=main action=block result=(CONSUME|SUCCESS) == 4
count \[cdevtest\] verb=use main=vintagedelight:salt_dust\*3 off=empty state="?minecraft:(ice|packed_ice)\b == 2
count \[cdevtest\] verb=state pos=30[03],-60,300 state="vintagedelight:salt\[layers=1\]" == 2
reject ^(?!.*RuntimeDistCleaner).*(Exception|/ERROR\]).*(salt|hearth|creativedelight|creativecommon|vintagedelight)
look before the ticks: ice and packed ice kept with a 1-layer salt layer above, dust 4 -> 3; snow 1 and 3: record (layer on top, or replaced); after the ticks: ice -> water, packed -> ice; layer above popped or kept (record)

## SQ-PS15-02 | dispenser with salt dust facing air over grass, air over air, ice, packed ice, snow layer, salt layer 3, stone
@group A
@commands Dispenser with salt dust facing air over grass; facing air over air; facing ice, packed ice, a snow layer; facing a salt layer of 3; facing a stone block. Then `[salt.Melting] SaltItemMeltingEnabled = false`, restart, facing ice
