@@sources feature_writeup/melting.md feature_writeup/plan_post_scratch_1115.md
@@text
@@text Creative Common built 2026-11-17 (lane M1, build/libs). Group A superflat, `gamerule randomTickSpeed 3` (the melt ticks are scheduled ticks, not random ticks; a high random tick speed hides the pace) unless a row says otherwise. Config `[melting]` in `config/creativecommon-common.toml`: `meltTickInterval 200`, `snowLayerMeltChance 0.8`, `magmaInstantRange 2`, `saltMeltSnowLayers 3`, `slowHeatMelting false`. Rows that need Immersive Weathering blocks use `immersive_weathering:cryosol` and `immersive_weathering:permafrost`.
@@text
@@table
## SQ-PS15-17 | snow melts one layer at a time beside a torch, at a steady pace; ice beside a torch still melts to water
@group A
@commands `setblock X -60 Z minecraft:snow[layers=8]` on stone, a `minecraft:torch` 2 blocks away (lit room); a second spot: `minecraft:ice` 2 from a torch. Probe the layer count with `cdevtest state` every 20 s for 4 minutes
@pass the layer count falls one at a time (8, 7, 6, ...; never a jump from several layers to air), first drop within about 70 s (target random tick or melt tick), then about one layer per 10 to 15 s; air within 4 minutes; the ice becomes `minecraft:water[level=0]` within 2 minutes
@fails whole stack gone at once: `meltedState` layer path; no change after the first drop: melt tick not scheduled (`hasScheduledTick`, mixin `m_222963_` not applied: grep latest.log for `MeltingBlockStateMixin`)
@draft runnable steps not written yet; the next runner writes them from @commands
## SQ-PS15-18 | a scheduled melt tick survives save and restart
@group A
@commands Snow `[layers=8]` 2 from a torch; wait for the first layer to go (SQ-PS15-17); `save-all`, `stop`, boot again on the same world, forceload the spot; probe the layer count every 20 s for 2 minutes
@pass layers keep falling after the restart without any random tick roll first (first drop within about 15 s of the chunk loading); no ERR at load naming block_ticks
@fails nothing for a minute, then a drop: the tick was not saved (only random ticks restarted it)
@draft runnable steps not written yet; the next runner writes them from @commands
## SQ-PS15-19 | magma: snow within 2 melts at once (placed and existing); snow at 3 melts by layer
@group A
@commands `minecraft:magma_block` on stone. (1) `setblock` `minecraft:snow[layers=4]` 1 above it and 2 to the side (distance 2); (2) a `minecraft:snow_block` and `minecraft:powder_snow` at distance 2; (3) `minecraft:snow[layers=8]` at distance 3. Wait 3 minutes
@pass (1) and (2) are air at once on placement (fizz); (3) loses layers one at a time and is gone within about 4 minutes; no snow ever stays at distance 2
@fails (1) stays: `onPlaced` magma path (`[melting] tags` line: magma count 1 or more); (3) gone at once: instant range read as fireRange
@draft runnable steps not written yet; the next runner writes them from @commands
## SQ-PS15-20 | magma: no snowfall and no freezing within 3; snow and ice form outside
@group B
@commands Snowy plains (or `/fillbiome` snowy_plains on a superflat area): a 16x16 stone floor with one magma block in the middle at floor level, a 5x5 water pool 1 block deep with magma under its center; `weather thunder 6000`; wait 10 minutes (snowfall is per chunk, not random tick speed)
@pass no snow layer on any block within 3 of the magma (sphere), snow layers elsewhere on the floor; the pool's water within 3 of the magma never turns to ice, the rest freezes
@fails snow near magma: `BiomeMeltMixin` not applied (`m_47519_`) or `magmaStopsFreezing` off; ice near magma: `m_47480_`
@draft runnable steps not written yet; the next runner writes them from @commands
## SQ-PS15-21 | snow on blue ice or IW permafrost ignores fire, lava and magma; salt still melts it
@group A
@commands `minecraft:snow[layers=8]` on `minecraft:blue_ice`, a torch 2 away and lava 3 away; the same on `immersive_weathering:permafrost`; the same on `minecraft:magma_block`-adjacent blue ice (magma 2 below the snow's side); a fourth stack on blue ice with a `salt:salt_block` touching it; wait 4 minutes
@pass the first three stacks still 8 layers (magma's instant melt skipped too); the salted stack loses layers (one per melt) and is gone within about 4 minutes
@fails heat melts the kept stacks: `keeps_snow` tag empty (`[melting] tags` line) or the check reads the wrong block; salted stack kept: salt path should ignore the rule
@draft runnable steps not written yet; the next runner writes them from @commands
## SQ-PS15-22 | packed ice, blue ice, cryosol, permafrost: no melting from fire, lava or magma; salt steps packed ice and cryosol only
@group A
@commands Boot log `[melting] random ticks on for 2 extra blocks`. Each block on stone with a torch, lava and magma touching it (one spot per block per source); a second set with a `salt:salt_block` touching each; wait 10 minutes
@pass every heat spot unchanged; salt: packed ice -> `minecraft:ice` (then water as ice does), cryosol -> `minecraft:dirt`; blue ice and permafrost unchanged
@fails a heat spot changed: `slowHeatMelting` on or the target path ignores it; salted packed ice unchanged: salt block not scanning on its own tick (salt blocks must random tick; Creative Delight SaltBlockTicks)
@draft runnable steps not written yet; the next runner writes them from @commands
## SQ-PS15-23 | salt dispenser removes 3 snow layers; a snow block becomes 5 layers; blue ice refused
@group A
@commands Dispenser with salt dust facing `minecraft:snow[layers=8]`; fire once, probe; fire again; then facing `minecraft:snow_block`, fire once; then facing `minecraft:blue_ice`, fire once
@pass 8 -> 5 -> 2 layers; snow block -> `minecraft:snow[layers=5]`; blue ice unchanged and the dispenser places a salt layer or drops the dust (Creative Delight's choice), no melt
@fails whole stack gone: `saltMeltSnowLayers` not used (Creative Delight calling an old path); blue ice melted: not saltable check
