@commands `weather rain`; an unlit campfire on stone under open sky, a second on `minecraft:coal_block` under open sky, an unlit soul campfire under open sky; right click each with a torch (the soul one with a soul torch); then `[campfire] torchRainRefuses = false` and retry the first
@pass first: stays unlit, extinguish (fizz) sound, torch kept; coal block one: lit, torch used; soul campfire: lit (rain never douses it); with the switch off: lit (then goes out after `rainOutTicks`)
@fails lit in rain: rule does not read `CampfireRain` tags; torch used though refused: order in `CampfireTorch`
